{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1336166-2nd-edition-equivalent-to-tongues-of-birds-and-words-of-wolves","id":1336166,"title":"2nd edition equivalent to \"Tongues of Birds and Words of Wolves\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-17T01:13:04-07:00","id":1336166,"title":"2nd edition equivalent to \"Tongues of Birds and Words of Wolves\"?","content":"First edition had Tongues of Birds and Words of Wolves as the first tier of the Fang and Talon contract and it seems like nothing equivalent made it into second edition.<br /> You can use Pipes of the Beastcallerof course, but there seems to be a definite lack of a low level power like they are available for Vampires, werewolves and Mages to communicate with animals.<br /> <br /> It is pretty easy of course to houserule one in, but I thought that it was a rather sad omission, given that it existed in the previous edition.<br /> <br /> If anyone else has already done a houseruled one, any suggestions for seeming benefits, loophole and regalia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","user":"Ray White","date":". 09-17-2019, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T07:50:58-07:00","id":1336210,"title":"","content":"You could always make it a seeming benefit...<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of Mirror:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Walls Have Ears (Common) </b><br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>The Grim can use this contract to speak with an animal instead of an object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T09:29:43-07:00","id":1336225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hedgebound Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1336166-2nd-edition-equivalent-to-tongues-of-birds-and-words-of-wolves?p=1336210#post1336210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always make it a seeming benefit...<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of Mirror:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Walls Have Ears (Common) </b><br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>The Grim can use this contract to speak with an animal instead of an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely not a bad suggestion, though I do think the overall mechanic of the contract might end up not having as much sensible application to animals.<br /> But thanks for the suggestion for sure!^^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: